WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.033
In this tutorial, Scenario Spark and an AI assistant work together.

2
00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:09.562
With a single prompt, you get a title, a narrative,

3
00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:14.998
a reflection on every course of action, and feedback from every persona.

4
00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:21.553
We start from the starter kit, and choose the scenario type Event safety.

5
00:00:21.903 --> 00:00:23.296
Open Create scenario.

6
00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:28.106
This box contains measures, so we turn on decision support.

7
00:00:28.456 --> 00:00:29.361
Click Generate.

8
00:00:29.411 --> 00:00:35.093
Spark picks a consistent option for every factor, and summarises the situation.

9
00:00:35.443 --> 00:00:38.279
Estimate the risk if nobody acts:

10
00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:41.647
a medium probability, with a high impact.

11
00:00:41.997 --> 00:01:02.981
Next, choose the measures for course of action A, and estimate the risk that remains.

12
00:01:03.331 --> 00:01:11.635
Duplicate it as course of action B, and change a few measures:

13
00:01:11.685 --> 00:01:19.292
a casualty collection point, a joint coordination team, and phased departure.

14
00:01:19.642 --> 00:01:21.532
Now click Ask LLM.

15
00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:25.411
One combined prompt asks for everything at once.

16
00:01:25.761 --> 00:01:33.267
Copy the prompt, and paste it into your AI assistant, for example Copilot in Microsoft Edge.

17
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:40.321
The assistant answers with a single JSON block.

18
00:01:40.371 --> 00:01:42.852
Copy the answer.

19
00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.917
Paste the JSON into the dialog.

20
00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:50.527
Spark checks it, and shows a preview of every part.

21
00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.753
Untick anything you don't want to use.

22
00:01:54.103 --> 00:01:55.043
Click Apply.

23
00:01:55.093 --> 00:01:59.001
The narrative is saved under the suggested title.

24
00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:01.250
Review the result.

25
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.499
The narrative remains fully editable.

26
00:02:04.849 --> 00:02:11.239
Each course of action now has its own reflection.

27
00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:16.053
And every persona describes how they experience the situation.

28
00:02:16.403 --> 00:02:21.436
Tick Select for analysis to add it to your saved scenarios.

29
00:02:21.486 --> 00:02:26.519
Now it also counts in the box and in decision support.

30
00:02:26.869 --> 00:02:31.972
In the morphological box, each category has its own tab.

31
00:02:32.022 --> 00:02:37.640
Coloured options show how often they are used in saved scenarios.

32
00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:43.759
The decision support page puts the courses of action side by side.

33
00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:53.180
Compare their measures, and see how each course of action lowers the risk in the risk matrix.

34
00:02:53.530 --> 00:03:02.600
Finally, record your decision and its rationale in the decision log.

35
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:10.023
Back on the home page, the saved scenario is ready to view, compare, or export.

36
00:03:10.373 --> 00:03:13.038
Want to redo just one part?

37
00:03:13.088 --> 00:03:17.110
Turn on Prompt per field in the LLM settings.

38
00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:23.445
Next to the all-in-one prompt, you then get a separate prompt for the narrative,

39
00:03:23.496 --> 00:03:25.708
each reflection, and each persona.

40
00:03:26.058 --> 00:03:26.970
That's it:

41
00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:32.261
from morphological box to a complete scenario in a few minutes.
